- **KEY DECISIONS THIS RUN:**
  1. **Symptom-subtype stratification (task #1656, P4):** ACKNOWLEDGED but NOT actionable. PMID 40367585 identifies distinctive PANS symptoms (separation anxiety, irritability, dysgraphia) but no available transcriptomic datasets have symptom-subtype labels. Current three-model strategy (combined/PANDAS/PANS classifiers, journal #1971) already addresses biological heterogeneity. Symptom subtypes are a future enhancement requiring labeled clinical data.
  2. **Keating proteomics/phosphoproteomics (task #1663, P3):** PRIDE PXD064184 now available — TMTpro 18-plex proteomics+phosphoproteomics, 18 PBMC samples (6 pre/6 post/6 control). HIGHEST PRIORITY use: phosphoproteomics validation of JAK-STAT enrichment (FE=12.4) from autoantibody project. Also feeds transcriptomic-biomarker-panel and IVIG mechanism. PM task #1750 issued to coordinate cross-project integration.
  3. **cDC cell-type refinement (task #1655, P3):** Li et al. PNAS 2024 (PMID 39254994) shows cGAS-STING pathogenicity is in classical DCs, NOT macrophages. CRITICAL refinement to two-hit model hit 2. Mechanistic chain updated: GAS → impaired clearance → persistent DNA → cDC cGAS-STING → type I IFN → T cell priming → autoimmunity. Macrophages reframed as effectors not initiators. PM task #1751 issued. Cross-project: ivig-mechanism scRNA-seq should prioritize cDC1/cDC2 populations.
  4. **TridentTCR endorsed as Layer 4 (task #1654, P3):** GNN+LLM TCR specificity predictor with autoimmune trinary classification. Closes the mimicry prediction loop: Layer 1 (peptide-MHC binding) → Layer 2 (structural mimicry) → Layer 3 (T-cell mimicry) → NEW Layer 4 (TCR recognition). T1D cross-reactivity precedent (ZnT8→gut mimotope) directly analogous to PANDAS. PM task #1752 issued.
- **CROSS-PROJECT CONVERGENCE UPDATE:** cDC refinement (two-hit) + phosphoproteomics (JAK-STAT validation) + TCR layer (mimicry pipeline) all strengthen the mechanistic picture. The cDC→T cell priming chain connects the two-hit model to the HLA-peptide project via antigen presentation.
